2
00:12:11,428 --> 00:12:17,428
Mortal Engines is a adventure, science fiction
film directed by Christian Rivers.

3
00:18:17,142 --> 00:18:23,142
Many thousands of years in the future, Earth’s cities roam the globe on huge wheels,
devouring each other in a struggle for ever diminishing resources.

4
00:24:22,857 --> 00:24:28,857
On one of these massive traction cities, the old London, Tom Natsworthy has an unexpected encounter with a
mysterious young woman from the wastelands who will change the course of his life forever.

5
00:30:28,571 --> 00:30:34,571
Hester Shaw, played by Hera Hilmar.

6
00:36:34,285 --> 00:36:40,285
Tom Natsworthy, played by Robert Sheehan.

7
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Thaddeus Valentine, played by Hugo Weaving.

8
00:48:45,714 --> 00:48:51,714
Anna Fang, played by Jihae.

9
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
Bevis Pod, played by Ronan Raftery.

10
01:00:57,142 --> 01:01:03,142
Katherine Valentine, played by Leila George.

11
01:07:02,857 --> 01:07:08,857
Mortal Engines is a 2018 post-apocalyptic steampunk
film, based on Philip Reeve's 2001 novel.

12
01:13:08,571 --> 01:13:14,571
Directed by Christian Rivers and written by Fran Walsh, Philippa Boyens, and Peter Jackson, it stars Hera Hilmar,
Robert Sheehan, Hugo Weaving, Jihae, Ronan Raftery, Leila George, Patrick Malahide, and Stephen Lang.

13
01:19:14,285 --> 01:19:20,285
An American–New Zealand co-production, the film is set in a post-apocalyptic world where entire
cities have been mounted on wheels and motorised, and practice municipal Darwinism.

14
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:26,000
Jackson purchased the rights to the book in 2009, but the film languished
for several years before being officially announced in 2016.

15
01:31:25,714 --> 01:31:31,714
Jackson picked Rivers, who won an Academy Award for Best Visual Effects for his work on Jackson's King Kong, to make his feature-length directorial debut
with the project, and also brought on several members of his production teams from The Lord of the Rings and The Hobbit film trilogies.

16
01:37:31,428 --> 01:37:37,428
Filming took place from April to July 2017 in New Zealand.

17
01:43:37,142 --> 01:43:43,142
Mortal Engines had its world premiere on November 27, 2018, in London, was theatrically released
in New Zealand on December 6, 2018, and in the United States on December 14, 2018.

18
01:49:42,857 --> 01:49:48,857
The film received mixed reviews from critics and is one of the biggest box office bombs of all time, grossing $84
million against a production budget of $100–150 million and losing Universal an estimated $175 million.

19
01:55:48,571 --> 01:55:54,571
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, dystopia,
post-apocalyptic future, revenge, wasteland.

20
02:01:54,285 --> 02:02:00,285
The tone is thought_provoking.
